//! The APV ANTC1608-103F3380FB chip NTC thermistor, 10 kohm at 25 C, 0603: TH1 (`NTC_CONV`) and
//! TH2 (`NTC_PLUG`) of the Power Manifold charger module (LCSC C52155402,
//! `catalogs/antc1608_ntc.csv`). It provides the standard `NtcThermistor`: two passive pins,
//! `.a` (pad 1) and `.b` (pad 2) (a thermistor is not polarized), and at DC a resistor over the
//! range of the maker's resistance-temperature table. The generic's letters are `RT` (IEEE 315),
//! so the port numbers the two RT1 and RT2; `reference/parts.toml` pairs them with TH1 and TH2.
//!
//! The figures are the catalog row's (`catalogs/antc1608_ntc.csv`, with the document, revision
//! and page): the zero-power resistance at 25 C with its tolerance, the table's resistance at
//! -40 C and at 125 C (the operating range's ends: APV "Chip NTC Thermistors, ANTC Series",
//! revised 2026-06-21, p.10, column 103x3380FB: 197.39 kohm and 0.532 kohm, centre values),
//! the two B constants, the rated power and the permissible operating current. The B
//! constants, the rated power and the current are data: no relation reads them (the power and
//! the current are figures at 25 C, `NtcThermistor`'s doc says why).

import std::parts::passive::NtcThermistor

/// A chip NTC thermistor with two terminals.
part Antc1608Ntc provides NtcThermistor {
    pins "0603" {
        .a passive "A" "1"
        .b passive "B" "2"
    }

    /// The B constants, in kelvin, as the datasheet gives them (25 C and 50 C; 25 C and 85 C).
    .b_constant_25_50: Temperature
    .b_constant_25_85: Temperature
    /// The rated electric power at 25 C.
    .rated_power: Power
    /// The permissible operating current at 25 C.
    .max_current: Current

    .mpn: String
    catalog antc1608_ntc by .mpn { .mpn, .package, .resistance_25c, .cold_resistance, .hot_resistance, .b_constant_25_50, .b_constant_25_85, .rated_power, .max_current }
}
